Subject: [PATCH 2/2] WS-07: lossless bulk-table round trip (review of ea67da2)

- Property columns are written as `properties.<key>` and read back as
  that property, so a property named `text`, `name`, `article`, `order`,
  `model` or `type` no longer lands on Description, Order number or Type
  number. A paste where two columns map to one field is refused
  (BulkError::DuplicateColumn) instead of the later column winning.
- find_device falls back to the product designation only when the pasted
  tag has no `=` or `+` levels, so `=ZZ9+ELSEWHERE-K1` no longer edits
  `=A1+CAB-K1`.
- to_tsv quotes cells holding tabs, line breaks or quotes RFC 4180 style
  instead of flattening them; parse_delimited already reads that.
- A cell that still shows the current value leaves it untouched, so an
  unchanged paste is a no-op even for values with surrounding spaces.
- CLAUDE.md: the crate is a property sheet model, not a panel.

Regression tests for each item.

